  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food Safety and Quality in Midday school meals</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project explores quality and standards problematics in the push towards remote and distributed mid-day school meal production and distribution, and actively curates and test new science based technologies and methodologies that will ensure the high nutritional and safe quality of the TAPF school meal, as well as ensure the sustainability of the production of Akshaya Patra, including in terms rural population empowerment, sourcing of sustainable (organic) raw materials and reduction of food waste.

The project aims to result in increased reach, quality and sustainability (including sustainability effects) of India&#x2019;s midday meal scheme.</narrative>
  </description>
